          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Synthesis of the Postulate System\n\nThe Counting-Iris Number System rests upon a finite, constructive foundation:\n\n. **Discrete Arithmetic Base (Postulates 0–1, 5, 7)**: The physical universe and mathematical calculation proceed strictly through finite discrete counting steps on multiscale resolution grids \\( \\mathcal { G } _ \\omega \\). Continua containing uncountably infinite point-sets are eliminated from linguistic and formal mathematical formulation.\n+\n. **Algebraic Geometry and Clifford Embedding (Postulates 2–4, 9)**: Multivector space \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\) provides the exact geometric container for physical fields, parity dualities, and Spin(2) bivector vortex structures generated by the Iris element \\( \\iota \\).\n+\n. **Observation and Main Scale Projection (Postulates 6, 8)**: Measurement operations over finite observation durations \\( \\tau _ { \\text { obs } } \\) map fine vernier readings \\( \\text { Fin } ( \\mathbb { R } ^ { \\ast } ) \\) onto standard real flux values via the Main Scale Projection operator \\( ( \\downarrow ) \\)."
