      "summary": "In this chapter, the Principle of Least Action (\\( \\delta S = 0 \\)) and variational principles are shown to be constructive, structural tautologies of multivector field momentum and energy conservation rather than empirical postulates or mysterious teleological \"minimizations\" of scalar quantities. By formulating the field action integral on the discrete multiscale grid \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\), variational principles are derived directly from first principles.",
