          "id": "sec-engineering-design-of-the-industrial-granular-calcining-plant",
          "title": "Engineering Design of the Industrial Granular Calcining Plant",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Engineering Design of the Industrial Granular Calcining Plant\n\nBuilding upon the agglomeration and calcination theorems, the practical manufacturing process incorporates three coupled equipment stages:\n\n. **Pre-Mixer and Rotary Agglomeration Drum**:\n   - A stainless steel inclined rotary cylinder equipped with high-pressure atomizing liquid spray nozzles delivering deionized water or recycle liquor onto a cascade of fine phosphate powder feed.\n   - Internal flighting ensures uniform particle showering and continuous turnover, maintaining aggregate diameter within the 20 to 100 mesh range (\\( 150\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\text{ to } 850\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\)).\n\n. **Direct-Fired Rotary Calciner**:\n   - A counter-current refractory-lined rotary kiln operating with gas or oil combustion burners, maintaining a controlled axial thermal profile from \\( 200^\\circ \\text{C} \\) at the feed inlet to \\( 450^\\circ \\text{C} \\text{--} 520^\\circ \\text{C} \\) at the discharge weir.\n   - Controlled draft ventilation removes water vapor without entraining fines, preserving granule integrity.\n\n. **Fluidized-Bed Granule Cooler and Classifier**:\n   - A counter-current vibrating fluid-bed cooler rapidly quenching the hot granular discharge to \\( T \\le 60^\\circ \\text{C} \\) with dry ambient air to freeze the crystal phase ratio and prevent moisture re-absorption.\n   - Vibratory multi-deck screens separate oversize material for gentle roll crushing and recycle undersize fines directly back to the agglomeration drum feed.\n\n[#chap-how-wings-work]"
