      "summary": "This chapter applies the Master Field Equation DF = J in Cl(4,1,1) to macro-scale astrophysics and cosmology. Grounded in a discrete multiscale spatial grid, the framework resolves core cosmological paradoxes without unobservable entities like dark matter, dark energy, or Big Bang creation singularities. We examine galactic vorticity and flat rotation curves, stellar nucleosynthesis, collapsed remnants (white dwarfs, neutron stars, and non-singular magnetoplasmoid kernels), the steady-state cosmic microwave background, and establish the physical optical visibility horizon of the universe.",
