          "title": "Summary Comparison: Forward Evolution vs. Backward Deduction",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "=== Summary Comparison: Forward Evolution vs. Backward Deduction\n\n[cols=\"2,3,3\", options=\"header\"]\n|===\n| Dimension | Forward Dynamical Evolution | Backward Abductive Deduction\n| **Direction** | Past \\( \\to \\) Future | Present Observation \\( \\to \\) Past Cause\n| **Mapping Characteristic** | Many-to-One (Dissipative Contraction) | One-to-Many (Pre-Image Tree Expansion)\n| **Geometric Structure** | Point trajectories settling onto attractors | Self-similar branching trees & Julia boundaries\n| **Combinatorial Nature** | Deterministic single path | Branching forest requiring aperture pruning\n| **Guiding Principle** | Master Field Equation \\( DF = J \\) | Jaynesian Inverse Probability & MaxEnt\n| **Optimal Algorithm** | Forward time-stepping (Runge-Kutta / Vernier) | Hierarchical tree pruning \\( \\mathcal { O } ( \\log N ) \\)\n|==="
