          "title": "Index of Formal Statements",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "== Index of Formal Statements\n\nThis index lists all formal Postulates, Theorems, and Definitions established across the textbook.\n\n=== Theorems\n\n* xref:thm-svd-hobby-least-squares[**Theorem: Universal Existence, Uniqueness, and Least-Squares Optimality of SVD-Hobby Splines in the Iris Number System**]  -- Chapter: *Smooth Spline Interpolation: Hobby’s Algorithm and its Extension via Singular Value Decomposition* | Section: *The SVD Extension: Finding the Best Harmony in Every Situation*\n* xref:thm-exact-circle-representation[**Theorem: Exact Conic Representation in \\( Cl(3,0) \\)**]  -- Chapter: *Symmetric Power Polynomials in Geometric Algebra: Points, Vectors, and the s-Power Basis* | Section: *The Homogeneous Model in \\( Cl(3,0) \\): Rational Curves and Exact Conics*\n* xref:thm-spower-arbitrary-degree[**Theorem: Complete S-Power Basis Representation for Arbitrary Degree \\( n \\)**]  -- Chapter: *Symmetric Power Polynomials in Geometric Algebra: Points, Vectors, and the s-Power Basis* | Section: *The s-Power Basis: Structural Separation of Points and Deviation Vectors*\n* xref:thm-spower-bivector-excursion[**Theorem: Exact Multivector Area and Bivector Deviation Bounds**]  -- Chapter: *Symmetric Power Polynomials in Geometric Algebra: Points, Vectors, and the s-Power Basis* | Section: *Geometric Algebra of Deviation: Wedge Products and Exact Enclosed Area*\n\n=== Definitions\n\n* xref:def-polar-form-cl20[**Definition: Symmetric Multilinear Blossom in \\( Cl(2,0) \\)**]  -- Chapter: *Symmetric Power Polynomials in Geometric Algebra: Points, Vectors, and the s-Power Basis* | Section: *Symmetric Polar Forms (Blossoming) in \\( Cl(2,0) \\)*\n* xref:def-affine-point-vector-split[**Definition: Affine Point–Vector Decomposition in \\( Cl(3,0) \\)**]  -- Chapter: *Symmetric Power Polynomials in Geometric Algebra: Points, Vectors, and the s-Power Basis* | Section: *Points Versus Vectors: The Foundational Geometric Distinction*\n\n"
